# Kernel cmdline parameters for launching the HostOS.
# BOOT_ARGS_A targets partition set "A" while BOOT_ARGS_B targets partition set "B"
#
# oops=panic panic=10: turn any kernel Oops into a panic and reboot 10 s later.
# softlockup_panic=1 watchdog_thresh=60: also panic when a CPU is stuck in the kernel for 120 s
# (twice watchdog_thresh). The default 20 s is too short: in system tests the HostOS itself runs
# virtualized, and a vCPU starved by an oversubscribed host looks stuck as well. The window cannot
# be longer: a stuck CPU reports an RCU stall itself every 180 s
# (3 x rcupdate.rcu_cpu_stall_timeout) and that report restarts the soft-lockup window.
# cpufreq.default_governor=performance: where the HostOS sets the CPUs' frequency (acpi-cpufreq; on
# most hosts the firmware does), keep them at full clock. With schedutil, the kernel's default,
# idle cores sit at the lowest P-state, and the replica's short CPU bursts end before the clock
# ramps up: per-round state hashing takes 1.7x as long.
BOOT_ARGS_A="root=/dev/hostlvm/A_root console=ttyS0,115200 console=tty0 nomodeset video=1024x768 oops=panic panic=10 softlockup_panic=1 watchdog_thresh=60 cpufreq.default_governor=performance dfinity.system=A lsm=lockdown,capability,landlock,yama,selinux,ima,evm selinux=1 enforcing=0"
BOOT_ARGS_B="root=/dev/hostlvm/B_root console=ttyS0,115200 console=tty0 nomodeset video=1024x768 oops=panic panic=10 softlockup_panic=1 watchdog_thresh=60 cpufreq.default_governor=performance dfinity.system=B lsm=lockdown,capability,landlock,yama,selinux,ima,evm selinux=1 enforcing=0"
